    <string name="meta_tab_everyone">Everyone</string>
    <string name="meta_tab_you">You</string>
    <string name="player_intro">Your career, looked up by BattleTag. There is no sign-in because there is nothing to sign in to: Blizzard publish no Overwatch API, so the only source is the career profile they publish for players who have set theirs to public. Type the whole tag — Name#1234 — to go straight to one.</string>
    <string name="player_battletag">BattleTag or name</string>
    <string name="player_search">Search</string>
    <string name="player_no_results">Not found. Try the whole BattleTag with its number, like Name#1234, which addresses a profile directly. If that fails too, the profile is almost certainly private: Blizzard only publishes — and only lets anything search — profiles set to public in the game, under Options, Social, Career Profile.</string>
